---
import DocPage from '../../components/DocPage.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
---
<DocPage eyebrow="DOCS / CI" title="GitHub Actions" lead="link1345/gua-tester provides versioned CI workflows for Gua UI tests in Godot 4.7 and Unity 6 projects." description="Godot and Unity inputs, credentials, artifacts, and visual reports provided by Gua Tester Actions." section="docs">
  <Callout title="Gua Tester Actions v2.2"><p>See <a href="https://github.com/link1345/gua-tester">link1345/gua-tester</a> for the implementation and releases. v2 moves the Godot all-in-one action from the repository root to <code>/godot</code> and adds the Unity reusable workflow.</p></Callout>

  <h2>Godot 4.7</h2>
  <p>The Godot composite action downloads the selected Windows Godot build, links the released Gua addon, exports <code>GODOT_EXECUTABLE</code>, prepares project imports, and runs the external <code>Gua.Testing.Godot</code> test project.</p>
  <CodeBlock title=".github/workflows/godot.yml" lang="yaml" code={`jobs:
  godot:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: link1345/gua-tester/godot@v2.2
        with:
          project-path: game
          test-project: tests/GuaTester.Tests.csproj
          godot-version: "4.7"
          godot-status: stable
          gua-plugin-tag: gua-v1.18.0`} />
  <div class="grid-2"><div class="mini-card"><strong>test-project (required)</strong><p>The <code>.csproj</code> that references <code>Gua.Testing.Godot</code>.</p></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>project-path</strong><p>Godot project path; default <code>game</code>.</p></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>godot-version / godot-status</strong><p>Default <code>4.7</code> and <code>stable</code>.</p></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>test-logger</strong><p>Default <code>trx;LogFileName=godot.trx</code>.</p></div></div>
  <p>The outputs are <code>godot-executable</code> and <code>addon-path</code>. Component actions remain available as <code>link1345/gua-tester/setup-godot@v2.2</code> and <code>link1345/gua-tester/link-gua-gdscript-addon@v2.2</code>.</p>

  <h2>Unity 6 Windows x64</h2>
  <p>The Unity reusable workflow installs a released Gua UPM package, builds a rendered Windows x64 Mono Player with GameCI on Linux, transfers the Player to a Windows runner, fixes its display at 1920x1080, and runs external NUnit tests with <code>GUA_UNITY_PLAYER</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock title=".github/workflows/unity.yml" lang="yaml" code={`jobs:
  unity:
    if: github.event_name != 'pull_request' || github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.repository
    uses: link1345/gua-tester/.github/workflows/unity.yml@v2.2
    with:
      project-path: game
      scene-path: Assets/Scenes/Title.unity
      test-project: tests/GuaTester.Unity.Tests.csproj
      artifact-key: game
      unity-version: auto
      gua-tag: gua-v1.18.0
    secrets:
      UNITY_EMAIL: \${{ secrets.UNITY_EMAIL }}
      UNITY_PASSWORD: \${{ secrets.UNITY_PASSWORD }}
      UNITY_LICENSE: \${{ secrets.UNITY_LICENSE }}
      UNITY_SERIAL: \${{ secrets.UNITY_SERIAL }}`} />
  <p>Required inputs are <code>project-path</code>, <code>scene-path</code>, <code>test-project</code>, and a caller-unique <code>artifact-key</code>. Optional inputs include <code>unity-version</code>, <code>gua-repository</code>, <code>gua-tag</code>, <code>dotnet-version</code>, <code>configuration</code>, <code>test-logger</code>, and <code>artifact-path</code>. <code>checkout-repository</code> and <code>checkout-ref</code> support fixtures in another repository. Use a matrix value for <code>artifact-key</code> when invoking the workflow more than once in a run.</p>
  <div class="grid-2"><div class="mini-card"><strong>Personal license</strong><p>Pass <code>UNITY_EMAIL</code>, <code>UNITY_PASSWORD</code>, and <code>UNITY_LICENSE</code>.</p></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>Professional license</strong><p>Pass <code>UNITY_EMAIL</code>, <code>UNITY_PASSWORD</code>, and <code>UNITY_SERIAL</code>.</p></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>Supported target</strong><p>Unity 6000.5+, Windows x64, Mono, rendered Player.</p></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>Artifacts</strong><p>Unity logs, Player files, TRX, diagnostics, and visual results.</p></div></div>
  <Callout kind="warn" title="Protect Unity credentials"><p>GitHub does not pass Actions secrets to fork pull requests. Skip this job for untrusted forks and do not use <code>pull_request_target</code> to execute untrusted game code with Unity credentials.</p></Callout>
  <Callout kind="tip" title="Keep Gua versions aligned"><p>Pin <code>gua-tag</code> and use the matching <code>Gua.Testing.Unity</code> NuGet version. The initial workflow does not support IL2CPP, non-Windows Players, Editor Play Mode CI, IMGUI, or EditorWindow automation.</p></Callout>

  <h2 id="visual-report">Visual difference reports</h2>
  <p><code>link1345/gua-tester/visual-report@v2.2</code> converts <code>Gua.Testing.Visual</code> manifests and PNGs into a static report for a workflow artifact or GitHub Pages. It is engine-neutral.</p>
  <CodeBlock title="Upload a failed visual report" lang="yaml" code={`- name: Upload visual report
  if: failure()
  uses: link1345/gua-tester/visual-report@v2.2
  with:
    artifact-path: artifacts/gua
    test-outcome: failure
    upload-target: workflow`} />
  <p>Set <code>upload-target</code> to <code>pages</code> only in a trusted main or manually dispatched run, then deploy the generated Pages artifact from a separate job with <code>pages: write</code> and <code>id-token: write</code>.</p>
  <Callout kind="warn" title="Screenshot visibility"><p>Screenshots may contain secrets or personal information rendered by the game. Review captured content before publishing reports.</p></Callout>

  <h2>Move from v1 to v2</h2>
  <p>Replace <code>link1345/gua-tester@v1</code> with <code>link1345/gua-tester/godot@v2.2</code>. There is no v2 root compatibility action. The Godot TRX default changes from <code>godot-gdscript.trx</code> to <code>godot.trx</code>.</p>
</DocPage>
